  "id": "pms",
  "term": "PMS",
  "definition": "PMS, or premenstrual syndrome, is a condition linked to the menstrual cycle in which hormonal changes interact with the brain’s stress and emotion-regulation systems. In the luteal phase, this interaction may increase stress sensitivity and is associated with affective, physical, and sleep-related symptoms, along with altered activity in emotion-related brain systems.",
